WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:10.664
Tiger ruled the jungle.

2
00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:16.486
He had sharp fangs, long claws, and smooth golden fur.

3
00:00:20.128 --> 00:00:23.309
When he roared, everyone trembled with fear.

4
00:00:23.329 --> 00:00:27.030
"Get out of my way!"

5
00:00:28.031 --> 00:00:29.111
Tiger roared.

6
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.201
Birds, monkeys, and other small animals scattered.

7
00:00:37.581 --> 00:00:40.162
But Water Buffalo was bigger than Tiger.

8
00:00:40.182 --> 00:00:43.523
"Don't tell me what to do."

9
00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:48.705
Water Buffalo walked right by and dipped into the lake.

10
00:00:53.466 --> 00:00:54.967
Tiger slashed a tree.

11
00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:59.448
"How can I make him listen to me?"

12
00:01:02.588 --> 00:01:05.689
A week later Tiger was roaming through the jungle.

13
00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:11.170
In one area all the trees were gone.

14
00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:15.832
Suddenly Tiger saw a new animal.

15
00:01:17.152 --> 00:01:20.313
It walked on two legs and cut down weeds.

16
00:01:24.054 --> 00:01:24.554
the plow!"

17
00:01:25.874 --> 00:01:27.475
it commanded another animal.

18
00:01:31.196 --> 00:01:32.316
Tiger gasped.

19
00:01:33.004 --> 00:01:34.525
"That's Water Buffalo!

20
00:01:35.665 --> 00:01:38.486
Why is he listening to that weak-looking animal?"

21
00:01:40.507 --> 00:01:42.468
The strange animal walked away.

22
00:01:44.509 --> 00:01:46.750
Tiger hurried over to Water Buffalo.

23
00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.491
"What's going on?

24
00:01:49.251 --> 00:01:50.371
Who is that?"

25
00:01:50.391 --> 00:01:55.454
"That's a human," Water Buffalo said.

26
00:01:55.474 --> 00:01:57.855
"He's farming the land."

27
00:01:59.835 --> 00:02:00.896
Tiger blinked.

28
00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.469
"Why do you listen to him?

29
00:02:04.309 --> 00:02:05.709
He's smaller than you.

30
00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:10.330
Plus he doesn't have claws or fangs."

31
00:02:12.511 --> 00:02:13.251
"That's true.

32
00:02:13.851 --> 00:02:17.792
But he has something more powerful," Water Buffalo said.

33
00:02:17.812 --> 00:02:20.253
"He has wisdom."

34
00:02:22.514 --> 00:02:24.054
Tiger rubbed his chin.

35
00:02:24.074 --> 00:02:27.715
"I need wisdom.

36
00:02:28.775 --> 00:02:31.296
Then everyone would listen to me."

37
00:02:35.504 --> 00:02:37.285
Tiger hurried after the human.

38
00:02:37.305 --> 00:02:44.631
"Hey!" The human spun around and trembled with fear.

39
00:02:47.813 --> 00:02:48.994
Tiger snarled.

40
00:02:49.014 --> 00:02:54.078
"Give me some wisdom!"

41
00:02:56.019 --> 00:02:57.320
The human gulped.

42
00:03:03.424 --> 00:03:06.527
"Okay. But I, um A sly grin slowly formed on his face.

43
00:03:06.547 --> 00:03:10.811
"I left it at home."

44
00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:15.735
Tiger snarled again.

45
00:03:15.755 --> 00:03:18.117
"Go and get it."

46
00:03:20.039 --> 00:03:20.519
"Yes, sir!"

47
00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.182
The human started to walk away but then stopped.

48
00:03:25.283 --> 00:03:26.224
He bit his lip.

49
00:03:28.306 --> 00:03:30.808
"You might eat my water buffalo while I'm away.

50
00:03:31.596 --> 00:03:33.858
Perhaps I can tie you to that tree?"

51
00:03:35.699 --> 00:03:36.660
Tiger sighed.

52
00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:41.363
"Fine. Just get me that wisdom."

53
00:03:41.383 --> 00:03:43.544
"Of course."

54
00:03:44.585 --> 00:03:46.046
The human grabbed a rope.

55
00:03:48.608 --> 00:03:50.829
He wrapped it around Tiger and the tree.

56
00:03:56.013 --> 00:03:56.513
be right back."

57
00:03:57.994 --> 00:04:00.096
The human walked away, whistling.

58
00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.882
The blazing sun heated up the rope.

59
00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:13.324
After an hour Tiger groaned.

60
00:04:17.087 --> 00:04:19.028
man tricked me."

61
00:04:20.569 --> 00:04:23.631
He tried to break free, but the rope was strong.

62
00:04:23.651 --> 00:04:28.754
For hours he struggled.

63
00:04:32.632 --> 00:04:36.875
The hot rope tightly rubbed against Tiger's fur, growing hotter.

64
00:04:38.416 --> 00:04:42.818
Smoke rose, and the smell of burning fur filled Tiger's nose.

65
00:04:49.041 --> 00:04:52.483
Finally Tiger broke free and darted to the lake.

66
00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.628
Then he saw his reflection.

67
00:05:01.984 --> 00:05:03.326
His fur was burnt!

68
00:05:03.346 --> 00:05:08.891
"I have stripes!"

69
00:05:08.951 --> 00:05:10.112
Tiger frowned.

70
00:05:10.132 --> 00:05:14.956
"But I did get some wisdom after all.

71
00:05:15.897 --> 00:05:18.099
Now I know not to trust humans!"
